<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/44387c61-f4c6-4c53-977f-572bec989213> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "One hand-written sort per element type — rejected: SLOP has no generics, so this multiplies the algorithm by the number of sorted types and guarantees the copies drift. Sorting an index permutation under a supplied comparator reduces each type to a six-line gather." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/456ce203-67b5-4e11-bed8-e4c2ebaa791d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Alternative> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/456ce203-67b5-4e11-bed8-e4c2ebaa791d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Import strlib.compare — rejected: implemented as strcmp over (. a data), so it assumes NUL termination that IRI slices out of a parsed Turtle buffer do not have. It would order entries by the bytes that happen to follow them in the file, making the sort a function of serialization rather than content." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/456ce203-67b5-4e11-bed8-e4c2ebaa791d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
