<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/eec8eb3f-b2d4-45ed-9351-3048d0831dd1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-20T14:54:51.521534Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/eec8eb3f-b2d4-45ed-9351-3048d0831dd1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Treat SWRL as inert, like annotations — rejected, and this is the dangerous option: 2 of RO's 25 rules derive owl:Nothing, so inert disposition would let an ontology whose authors encoded an incoherence be reported coherent. That is the exact fail-silent hazard §5.1 exists to prevent." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/f8becc95-31dc-43f9-a3ea-ac9f806b976c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Alternative> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/f8becc95-31dc-43f9-a3ea-ac9f806b976c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Implement DL-safe SWRL — rejected: decidable, but outside the cited EL++ completeness proofs so it would need its own, and restricting variables to named individuals changes what the author's rules mean. It also buys little: only 12 of RO's 25 rules genuinely need rule expressivity, and 6 are already expressible as v0 role chains." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/f8becc95-31dc-43f9-a3ea-ac9f806b976c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
