<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/f8becc95-31dc-43f9-a3ea-ac9f806b976c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-20T14:54:51.521534Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/f8becc95-31dc-43f9-a3ea-ac9f806b976c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Implement DL-safe SWRL — rejected: decidable, but outside the cited EL++ completeness proofs so it would need its own, and restricting variables to named individuals changes what the author's rules mean. It also buys little: only 12 of RO's 25 rules genuinely need rule expressivity, and 6 are already expressible as v0 role chains." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/00683550-a89a-4865-8633-222f7600d5e6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/00683550-a89a-4865-8633-222f7600d5e6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SWRL is out-of-profile at every rung, never implemented" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/00683550-a89a-4865-8633-222f7600d5e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/00683550-a89a-4865-8633-222f7600d5e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "SWRL rules are dispositioned **out-of-profile and enumerated** in SPEC.md §5.2, and will not be implemented at v0, v1 or v2. This is a settled position, not a deferral.\n\nWHY NOT IMPLEMENT. SWRL is a 2004 W3C Member *Submission*, never a Recommendation, and is in neither OWL 2 DL nor OWL 2 EL — so omitting it costs nothing against the completeness claim, and ELK does not support it either. Decisively: **unrestricted SWRL is undecidable**, so implementing it would forfeit §3.1's claim to be sound and complete for a NAMED logic, which is the entire basis for calling HOWL a DL reasoner rather than a materialization engine. DL-safe SWRL is decidable but sits outside the cited EL++ completeness results (it would need its own proof) and silently restricts rule variables to named individuals, changing what the author's rules mean.\n\nWHY ENUMERATED RATHER THAN INERT — this is the part that matters. Measured on RO, which ships 25 SWRL rules: 6 are plain v0 role chains written as rules rather than `owl:propertyChainAxiom`; 5 require inverses (v1); 12 are class-guarded chains no DL on the roadmap expresses; and **2 derive `owl:Nothing`** — they are unsatisfiability conditions, exactly what `validate` exists to catch. Treating SWRL as inert would let an ontology whose authors ENCODED an incoherence come back `coherent`. Enumerated, `coverage.omitted` is non-empty and the run is inconclusive: HOWL says it could not check completely, which is true.\n\nTHE LINT OPPORTUNITY. Since 6 of 25 are role-chain-shaped, the omission diagnostic should report whether an equivalent v0 axiom exists, turning a dead end into advice for the ontology author. HOWL must never perform that rewrite itself — transforming input to enlarge coverage would break §6.8's input-determined reports and decide a modelling question belonging to the ontology's owner.\n\nWHERE RULES GO IF EVER WANTED. DL-safe rules are Datalog, and GROWL is already a forward-chaining OWL 2 RL materializer. The §8.2 composition seam (HOWL classifies → GROWL materializes) gives rules a home without touching HOWL's calculus or its completeness claim.\n\nHOW IT WAS FOUND: empirically, not by review. A construct census over candidate corpus ontologies hit `swrl:Imp` in RO and found §5.2's disposition table had no row for it — and the table is specified as a total function over recognized constructs, so an absent row is a spec bug by the spec's own rule. Fixed in the same pass.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §5.2 (SWRL row and the note following it); corpus/fixtures/out-of-profile/swrl-rule.ttl; corpus/census.py." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/00683550-a89a-4865-8633-222f7600d5e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
