<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/00683550-a89a-4865-8633-222f7600d5e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/6db03a02-b135-48eb-b409-f484614cc58a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/00683550-a89a-4865-8633-222f7600d5e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/73f4c2dc-b853-4a94-8db2-56ac1828755b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/00683550-a89a-4865-8633-222f7600d5e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/eec8eb3f-b2d4-45ed-9351-3048d0831dd1> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/00683550-a89a-4865-8633-222f7600d5e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/f8becc95-31dc-43f9-a3ea-ac9f806b976c> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/17beb51b-607b-4ff3-99de-b2afbb9dc801> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/17beb51b-607b-4ff3-99de-b2afbb9dc801> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "HOWL and GROWL compose through RDF, never shared state" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/17beb51b-607b-4ff3-99de-b2afbb9dc801> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/17beb51b-607b-4ff3-99de-b2afbb9dc801> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The two engines never touch each other's memory. HOWL classifies and emits inferred subClassOf axioms as RDF; GROWL materializes and enriches over the enlarged schema. Everything crossing the boundary is RDF — the first two pipeline stages (parse, RDF-to-axiom) and the last (emit Turtle) ARE the composition seam.\n\nWhy: it keeps GROWL stable and production-safe while HOWL evolves, and it lets either engine run standalone. The two are complementary rather than competing — GROWL materializes OWL 2 RL (sound, deliberately incomplete for OWL-DL, best at enrichment and bulk ABox work), HOWL classifies a named description logic (sound AND complete for its fragment, best at defined-class subsumption and coherence of definitions and mappings).\n\nCorollary on sequencing: do not pre-refactor GROWL. Leaving it untouched is deliberate — the first move WHEN HOWL WORK STARTS is to lift the shared substrate (Turtle parse/serialize, Term/IRI/blank-node interning, IndexedGraph and arena utilities, the fixpoint control skeleton, worker pool and config plumbing) into a common library. Not copy-paste, and not a speculative refactor now.\n\nThe relationship is not purely one-directional, though. The consumer's pipeline runs an agreement stage that cross-checks the TBox and ABox engines on a deterministic probe set IN THE EL-INTERSECT-RL ENTAILMENT OVERLAP, where disagreement is an ENGINE FAULT and is never resolved by preferring one engine. So HOWL and GROWL are also independent oracles checked against each other in production: differential testing stops being a CI activity and becomes a live mechanism, and agreement with GROWL on the overlap becomes a standing correctness obligation.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §1 (the complementary-services table), §8.1 (shared vs. new), §8.2 (composition), §8.3 (do not pre-refactor), §8.4 (dual-engine cross-check), §10 test 19." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/17beb51b-607b-4ff3-99de-b2afbb9dc801> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
