<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/83481302-01ca-452f-82a5-b6dc3f338b97> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/d35faa16-fd37-4512-8d84-d27f47d463ff> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/83481302-01ca-452f-82a5-b6dc3f338b97> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/05b19f8b-f760-4d3b-a9c8-26a5c16da4f2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/85e6f9fb-40ea-497b-b689-3074f1a4ad52> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/85e6f9fb-40ea-497b-b689-3074f1a4ad52> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Consequence-based saturation, not tableau" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/85e6f9fb-40ea-497b-b689-3074f1a4ad52> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/85e6f9fb-40ea-497b-b689-3074f1a4ad52> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL derives entailed axioms FORWARD, saturating a set of consequences to a fixpoint, rather than refuting by constructing and branching a model. The calculus family is fixed at consequence-based (CB); only the fragment is staged.\n\nWhy CB:\n- CB IS a fixpoint. GROWL's `engine-run` — semi-naive delta iteration with dedup, worker fan-out, iteration cap, cancellation — is already the right control skeleton. The fact type changes (Triple becomes Derived), the loop does not.\n- Tableau requires model construction, non-deterministic case splits, backtracking, and blocking for termination. None of that fits SLOP's forward-fixpoint model or its Z3 weakest-precondition contract posture, under which each rule must be a pure function from premises to emitted conclusions.\n- Modern performance lives in CB: ELK (EL, massively parallel), Sequoia (CB SROIQ), Konclude (saturation-heavy hybrid, the ORE performance leader).\n- CB decomposes naturally into CONTEXTS, one per concept, which maps directly onto GROWL's fork-join worker model — the decomposition that makes context-owned state and the ownership invariant possible.\n\nThe fragment roadmap rides on this choice: v0 ELH⊥R+ with domain/range, v1 Horn-SHIQ (still Horn, still deterministic saturation, no clause branching), v2 SROIQ object fragment. The discontinuity is isolated at v2, where non-Horn requires first-class disjunctive clauses and ordered resolution; the Horn shapes of Derived/NormAxiom are the deterministic special case those generalize from. Design for v2 by not walling it off; do not build for it now.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §4 (Calculus: consequence-based saturation), §5 (Fragment roadmap), §6.5, §6.6." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/85e6f9fb-40ea-497b-b689-3074f1a4ad52> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/85e6f9fb-40ea-497b-b689-3074f1a4ad52> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-17T22:27:57.932665Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
