<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3f19adcf-2201-4823-9e5b-08dd02cf85e4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "missing-declaration-cmp compares the `referring` lists element-wise and therefore ASSUMES both are already sorted, which is the field invariant types.slop states. Every construction site must honour it; comparing two unsorted lists element-wise is not an order at all." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/430f1dda-868a-4168-ae0f-a343300284db> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/430f1dda-868a-4168-ae0f-a343300284db> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Queue list order is bucket order and is not content-canonical, so it must never escape into a report. It does not, because `classify.extract-findings` is the only path out — which makes that function's canonical ordering a determinism obligation rather than a tidiness one." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
