<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/844c16aa-2b1c-4d42-9997-0c9b078b65d2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-11T00:41:33.136149Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/844c16aa-2b1c-4d42-9997-0c9b078b65d2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Barriers idle workers that finish a round early — slower than pure ELK-style racing saturation, accepted as the price of a decision-bearing iteration cap." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8ce27e95-c717-484e-a281-01dabfac330e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8ce27e95-c717-484e-a281-01dabfac330e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GROWL's fixpoint control skeleton is copied intent rather than reinvented, making the shared-substrate boundary (generic driver vs. reimplemented skeleton) a live design question." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8ce27e95-c717-484e-a281-01dabfac330e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
