<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b0e575c2-5fbb-4c9b-ae27-b17b7f9ab42d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c7023d3a-4a30-4a92-a859-b1dcbb5819ed> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b293cf6e-d681-41a0-a895-fbe9eb20d4b7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b293cf6e-d681-41a0-a895-fbe9eb20d4b7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Differential oracles must be capability-probed per construct" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b293cf6e-d681-41a0-a895-fbe9eb20d4b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/17beb51b-607b-4ff3-99de-b2afbb9dc801> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b293cf6e-d681-41a0-a895-fbe9eb20d4b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b293cf6e-d681-41a0-a895-fbe9eb20d4b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "A reference reasoner counts as an oracle only for the constructs it is PROVEN to process, verified by probe at harness startup. An oracle that fails a construct's probe is not an oracle for that construct, and comparisons involving it are routed elsewhere.\n\nThe concrete exposure: ELK describes itself as implementing A FRAGMENT OF OWL 2 EL, and object-property ranges have historically been outside it — while v0 admits ranges. Run against an ELK that silently ignores a range axiom and a correct range-derived subsumption is reported as a HOWL EXTRA: a false fail in the acceptance suite, blamed on the implementation rather than the oracle. The unconditional \"any ontology HOWL accepts, ELK accepts\" of an earlier draft is not something this spec can assert about someone else's release, and it is load-bearing enough that an implementer trusting it would certify HOWL against an oracle that processed a different theory.\n\nRequired harness discipline:\n- Pin exact ELK and HermiT versions in the repo, alongside the corpus pins.\n- Capability-probe every v0 construct against each oracle at startup — one fixture per construct whose expected entailment the oracle must produce.\n- Fail the harness on any oracle warning or ignored-axiom diagnostic rather than diffing through it.\n- Route range-bearing cases to a confirmed-complete reasoner (HermiT, or ELK only if the pinned version passes the range probe); range-bearing fixtures are mandatory at M1, not avoided.\n\nTwo comparison rules travel with it. Compare the ENTAILMENT PREDICATE `entails-sub(A,B)`, not serialized taxonomies — HOWL's taxonomy is deliberately bottom-compressed, so diffing it against an oracle's entailment closure reports a mismatch on every corpus entry with an unsatisfiable class, a correct implementation failing its own acceptance test for representational reasons. And compare over ALL ordered pairs of named input classes for acceptance: a \"fixed probe set\" that is any proper subset lets a reasoner omit every entailment outside it and still be certified complete. Sampled probe sets are for production cross-checks only.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §10 item 1 (differential testing), §5.2 (the ELK-oracle paragraph), §12 M1 acceptance (b)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b293cf6e-d681-41a0-a895-fbe9eb20d4b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b293cf6e-d681-41a0-a895-fbe9eb20d4b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-17T22:26:57.517816Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
